convertible-helper (1.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Auto-rotate for tablets whose desktop does not rotate by itself: an
    [autorotate] profile section names the accelerometer (iio device name);
    while the tablet counts as in tablet mode the helper reads it from sysfs
    and sets the built-in display to the matching orientation, with a short
    settling delay and no change while the tablet lies flat.

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:00:00 -0700

convertible-helper (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The rotation and "security" button actions are now named per machine in a
    [buttons] profile section (rotate = KEY_PROG3, security = KEY_PROG1); the
    helper no longer acts on those keys anywhere else.  This stops the
    Toughpad FZ-G1's A1 button (KEY_PROG1) from opening the log-out dialog.

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:00:00 -0700

convertible-helper (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Tablets without a tablet-mode switch: optional profile files
    (/usr/share/convertible-helper/profiles/*.conf, /etc/convertible-helper.d)
    name the USB id of the dock keyboard; while it is detached the tablet
    counts as in tablet mode (keyboard setting on, screen reset on re-dock).

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:30:00 -0700

convertible-helper (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: resets the screen to normal when a convertible leaves
    tablet mode; handles the Toughbook CF-19 rotation and security buttons
    in any shell state. Replaces the GNOME Shell code that did this.
  * Enables the on-screen keyboard setting in tablet mode (restored on
    leaving it), through the public accessibility setting.

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:00:00 -0700
